      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '    SINCE UNRETIRING LATE LAST YEAR, SCC DIRECTOR AND RETIRED ADMIRAL
    WALTER GILROY HAS BEEN DOCUMENTING HIS LIFE STORY DURING HIS SPARE TIME. STARTING
    WITH HIS FIRST ASSIGNMENT AS AN ENSIGN CREWMATE IN 2164 ABOARD THE U.S.S. PULINSKI,
    GILROY DISCUSSES WHAT IT''S LIKE TO ASCEND THE LADDER OF COMMAND IN THE ESTEEMED
    SCC FLEET. HIS MEMOIR, WHICH IS CURRENTLY OVER 500 PAGES IN LENGTH, BEGINS WITH
    A SERIES OF ADVENTUROUS ENCOUNTERS RANGING FROM HANDLING TIME VORTEXES, TO ESCAPING
    BLACK HOLES, TO NEGOTIATING ALIEN ENCOUNTERS, AND BEYOND. '
