  m_text: "    GILROY SPOKE ON COMPLAINTS ABOUT THE CONTINUED DELAY OF PLANETARY
    COLONIZATION: \"I LOVE OUR SET OF DEEP SPACE STATIONS. I CONSIDER THOSE SPACE
    COLONIZATION. LOOK, WE'VE LANDED ON PLANETS BEFORE, BUT WE'RE NOT ALL THE WAY
    THERE YET TECHNOLOGICALLY. IF YOU WANT TO KNOW HOW WE GET THERE, I HAVE AN ANSWER
    FOR YOU: HUMAN CREW REPLACEMENT PROGRAM. WE NEED TO STREAMLINE OUR EXPLORATION,
    AND THE HCRP DOES THAT.\"\n    DEEP SPACE THIRTEEN WILL BE USED FOR RECREATION,
    REPAIRS, RESEARCH, AND DIPLOMATIC VENTURES. THE CHOSEN LOCATION PUTS IT IN VIEW
    OF ONE OF THE MOST FAMOUS NEBULAS, THE CHAMBERS NEBULA. "
