      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "    LUCKY THIRTEEN? SCC DIRECTOR WALTER GILROY HOPES SO. HIS ANNOUNCEMENT
    OF THE NEW DEEP SPACE STATION CAME AS A SURPRISE TODAY BUT CONTINUES THE TREND
    OF MAJOR ANNOUNCEMENTS SINCE HIS RETURN AS SCC DIRECTOR.\n    DEEP SPACE THIRTEEN
    IS EXPECTED TO BE THE BIGGEST OF THE REMOTE SPACE STATIONS, WITH A MAXIMUM OCCUPANCY
    OF 500 INDIVIDUALS, FIVE SHIP GATES, AND 20 DECKS. IT WILL ALSO BE THE FURTHEST
    IN DEEP SPACE YET. DEVELOPMENT IS EXPECTED TO TAKE ONE YEAR WITH AN ADDITIONAL
    YEAR OF CONSTRUCTION AND MATERIAL TRANSPORT. GILROY SAYS THE HCRP (HUMAN CREW
    REPLACEMENT PROGRAM) WILL ACCELERATE PROGRESS. "
